RESUME SKILL GAP ANALYZER - MULTI-CATEGORY SKILL MATCHING SYSTEM
================================================================

1. OVERVIEW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Complete resume skill matching system with:
- 14 job categories
- Core vs Supporting skill classification
- Synonym support (JS = JavaScript, etc.)
- Category-based filtering
- Strict scoring logic


2. JOB CATEGORIES & SKILLS STRUCTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2.1 Software Development
Core: JavaScript, Python, Java, C++, React, Node.js, Django, APIs, DSA
Supporting: SQL, MongoDB, Git, OOP

2.2 Web Development
Core: HTML, CSS, JavaScript
Supporting: Bootstrap, Tailwind, SEO, Responsive Design

2.3 Mobile Development
Core: Kotlin, Java, Swift, Flutter, React Native
Supporting: Firebase, APIs

2.4 UI/UX Design
Core: Figma, Adobe XD
Supporting: Wireframing, Prototyping, User Research

2.5 Data Science & Analytics
Core: Python, R, SQL
Supporting: Excel, Power BI, Tableau, Statistics

2.6 AI / Machine Learning
Core: Python, TensorFlow, PyTorch
Supporting: NLP, Deep Learning

2.7 Cloud Computing
Core: AWS, Azure, GCP
Supporting: Docker, Kubernetes, Linux

2.8 Cybersecurity
Core: Networking, Kali Linux
Supporting: Metasploit, Cryptography

2.9 Database Engineering
Core: SQL (advanced), Database Design
Supporting: Hadoop, Spark, ETL

2.10 DevOps
Core: Docker, Kubernetes, CI/CD
Supporting: Bash, Python, Terraform

2.11 Networking / IT Support
Core: Networking (LAN/WAN), Linux
Supporting: Troubleshooting, Windows

2.12 Game Development
Core: Unity, Unreal, C#, C++
Supporting: Game Physics, Animation

2.13 QA / Testing
Core: Manual Testing, Selenium
Supporting: Cypress, JIRA, Test Cases

2.14 Project Management
Core: Agile, Scrum
Supporting: Jira, Trello, Communication


3. SCORING LOGIC
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3.1 Core Skill Priority
- Core skills have HIGH weight (10% per skill)
- Supporting skills have MEDIUM weight (5% per skill)

3.2 Base Score Rule
IF at least ONE core skill matches:
   Base Score = 50-60%

IF no core skill matches:
   Score = 0-20% ONLY

3.3 Skill Match Boost
- Each additional matched core skill: +10%
- Each supporting skill: +5%

3.4 Max Score
- Cap score at 100%

3.5 Semantic Control
- Semantic similarity allowed ONLY if core skill matched
- Otherwise semantic score = 0

3.6 Final Scoring Formula
IF core_match:
   score = base_score + (core_matches x 10) + (support_matches x 5)
ELSE:
   score = 0-20


4. SYNONYM SUPPORT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Supported abbreviations and variations:
- JS = JavaScript
- Py = Python
- API = REST APIs
- React = React.js
- Node = Node.js
- ML = Machine Learning
- DL = Deep Learning
- NLP = Natural Language Processing
- AWS/Azure/GCP = Cloud platforms
- CI/CD = Jenkins, DevOps


5. GENERIC WORDS REMOVED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Words ignored during matching:
project, system, team, work, application, experience,
developed, created, managed, led, skills, knowledge,
proficient, communication, design, build, implement, etc.


6. OUTPUT FORMAT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
{
    "category": "software",
    "category_name": "Software Development",
    "detected_skills": ["JavaScript", "Python", "React"],
    "matched_core_skills": ["JavaScript", "Python", "React"],
    "matched_supporting_skills": ["Git"],
    "missing_core_skills": ["C++", "Django"],
    "missing_supporting_skills": ["SQL", "MongoDB"],
    "final_score": 85
}


7. TEST RESULTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

TEST 1: Data Entry -> Data Science
--------------------------------
Resume: Excel, Spreadsheet experience
Matched: Excel (supporting only)
Core: [] (no Python/R/SQL)
Score: 13/100
Result: LOW (correct - no core data science skills)

TEST 2: Software Developer -> Software Dev
-----------------------------------------
Resume: JavaScript, Python, Java, React, Node.js, Django, APIs, DSA, Git
Matched: 7 core + 1 supporting
Core: JavaScript, Python, Java, React, Node.js, Django, APIs
Score: 100/100
Result: HIGH (correct - multiple core skills)

TEST 3: Graphic Designer -> Software Dev
---------------------------------------
Resume: Photoshop, Illustrator, Figma, design team lead
Matched: [] (no software skills)
Core: []
Score: 0/100
Result: VERY LOW (correct - wrong domain)

TEST 4: Web Developer -> Web Dev
--------------------------------
Resume: HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Bootstrap, Tailwind, SEO, Responsive
Matched: 3 core + 4 supporting
Core: HTML, CSS, JavaScript
Score: 95/100
Result: HIGH (correct - all core + supporting)


8. KEY FEATURES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Category-based matching only
- Core skill priority enforcement
- No false positives for wrong domains
- Synonym expansion
- Generic word filtering
- Edge case handling (empty resume, no skills)


9. API USAGE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
from app.skill_matching import analyze_resume

result = analyze_resume(
    resume_text="JavaScript Python React developer",
    category="software",
    semantic_score=50
)

print(result["final_score"])
print(result["matched_core_skills"])


